pokeplatinum-speed-spd3.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the port's Save speed and battle intro hooks
(docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"); the Text speed hook is pokeplatinum-speed.patch. Each hook asks
port/game/speed_gen4_spd3.c, which reads the same settings Black's and Black 2's stand-ins read. At every default setting each
hook does nothing the game's own code did not do, so the route chain's frames are unchanged (both are pacing windows anyway: they
run libntr's tick timeline faster, never a game frame).
Save speed: scrcmd.c ScrCmd_258 (the save script's player pose, common.s CommonScript_StartSave: after the player's last Yes/No
answer and the "saving" message) opens the save window and ScrCmd_CloseSaveInfo (the script's last command, also the error path's)
closes it: the pose, the write, the saved message, the save jingle and the wait for A run at Save speed; the Yes/No questions do not.
The start menu's Save (start_menu.c StartMenu_Save) and every scripted save (a save script, the Battle Frontier's) run that script.
Battle intro (its hunk is in pokeplatinum-speed-spd2.patch, whose field_transition.c hunk sits at the same place):
field_transition.c FieldTask_RunEncounterEffect (the field task that plays the encounter's screen effect, in the field
overlay, before the battle's overlay loads) opens the battle window at its start and closes it when the effect is done.
